# Local tooling
# `.claude/` was ignored wholesale, yet five files under it are tracked —
# ARCHITECTURE_MAP.md, COMMON_MISTAKES.md, QUICK_START.md and the two READMEs —
# and CLAUDE.md points contributors at the first three as the project's key
# documents. An ignore rule cannot untrack what is already tracked, so those
# five kept working and nothing looked wrong; but anything NEW written beside
# them was silently invisible to `git status` and never reached the repo (F83).
# So the local scratch is named instead of the whole directory.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/agents/
.claude/completions/*
!.claude/completions/README.md
.claude/sessions/*
!.claude/sessions/README.md
.playwright-mcp/
.agents/
skills-lock.json
training-log-*.json

# Test coverage output (regenerable via `npm run test:coverage`)
coverage/
reports/
stryker-setup-*.js

# Playwright run artifacts — per-failure screenshots, videos and traces, plus a
# .last-run.json receipt. `.last-run.json` used to be TRACKED, and its committed
# copy read {"status":"passed"} in a repo where the suite did not pass and
# nothing ran it: a stale green receipt anyone could read and believe.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Hermes agent worktrees — worker checkouts, never committed
.worktrees/

# Python bytecode. A .pyc for scripts/migrate-history.py was tracked for
# months — machine-specific, regenerated on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
